Keep the BrowsingInstance across navigations in single-process OHOS.

A phone runs Chromium single-process: every page shares the one in-process
renderer with Chromium's own WebUI (the omnibox popup, chrome:// pages), so
that process always holds WebUI bindings. ShouldSwapBrowsingInstances-
ForNavigation counted the process's bindings as the current page being
WebUI, and since an ordinary page is never acceptable for WebUI, every
main-frame navigation forced a security BrowsingInstance swap. Measured on
device (chrome://process-internals): a.html in BI 33, the page it opened
with window.open() in BI 34 after loading. The swap severs window.opener,
so the opened page could not postMessage back and "Sign in with Google"
popups never completed. In single-process mode the process bindings are no
longer counted; whether the current page is WebUI is still checked.

Generated against Chromium 154.0.8037.51 with chromium-154-harmonyos.patch
applied. Apply with:
  git apply ohos-single-process-keep-browsing-instance.patch

diff --git a/content/browser/renderer_host/render_frame_host_manager.cc b/content/browser/renderer_host/render_frame_host_manager.cc
index f840f24..5210e0a 100644
--- a/content/browser/renderer_host/render_frame_host_manager.cc
+++ b/content/browser/renderer_host/render_frame_host_manager.cc
@@ -2833,8 +2833,24 @@ RenderFrameHostManager::ShouldSwapBrowsingInstancesForNavigation(
 
   // For security, we should transition between processes when one is a Web UI
   // page and one isn't, or if the WebUI types differ.
-  if (ChildProcessSecurityPolicyImpl::GetInstance()->HasWebUIBindings(
-          render_frame_host_->GetProcess()->GetDeprecatedID()) ||
+  bool current_process_has_webui_bindings =
+      ChildProcessSecurityPolicyImpl::GetInstance()->HasWebUIBindings(
+          render_frame_host_->GetProcess()->GetDeprecatedID());
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_OHOS)
+  // A phone runs single-process: every page shares the one in-process
+  // renderer with Chromium's own WebUI (the omnibox popup, chrome:// pages),
+  // so that process always holds WebUI bindings and they say nothing about
+  // this frame. Counting them sent every main-frame navigation down the
+  // WebUI branch below, where an ordinary page is never "acceptable for
+  // WebUI", so every navigation swapped BrowsingInstance -- which severs
+  // window.opener: a page opened with window.open() lost its opener as soon
+  // as it loaded, and "Sign in with Google" popups could not report back.
+  // Whether the current page itself is WebUI is still checked.
+  if (RenderProcessHost::run_renderer_in_process()) {
+    current_process_has_webui_bindings = false;
+  }
+#endif
+  if (current_process_has_webui_bindings ||
       WebUIControllerFactoryRegistry::GetInstance()->UseWebUIForURL(
           browser_context, current_effective_url)) {
     // If so, force a swap if destination is not an acceptable URL for Web UI.
